ate under T; no distinct residual function is required.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Lorck addresses Constance during an unwanted declaration after she has recoiled from his advances and asked him not to frighten her. He insists that his love is serious, then separately offers her himself, his life, and his soul. Constance immediately rejects the appeal and retreats.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression itself contains no clear undertaking. In the immediately following, separate offer, Lorck says, \\\"Jeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl\\\" and asks whether Constance will accept it. This figurative, totalizing offer has unclear practical terms and is expressly rejected by her: \\\"Nej, uf nej\\\".\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied evidence identifies the work as Amalie Skram's Constance Ring. No plot information beyond the supplied blocks was used.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence supports classifying the represented utterance and its immediate uptake, but it does not fully settle the sincerity, durability, or precise practical content of Lorck's professed devotion. Some source text also shows OCR or transcription irregularities.\"}"
